  "instructions": [
    "Toss the cabbage and carrot with the lime juice, olive oil, 1/4 tsp salt, and honey in a large bowl. Set aside while you cook the fish.",
    "Pat the cod dry with paper towels. Mix the cumin, paprika, garlic powder, 3/4 tsp salt, and pepper, then rub it over both sides of the fish.",
    "Heat the avocado oil in a 12 inch nonstick skillet over medium-high heat until it shimmers.",
    "Add the cod and cook 3 to 4 minutes, until the underside is golden and releases easily from the pan.",
    "Flip the fish and cook 2 to 3 minutes more, until it flakes easily and reaches 145 F in the thickest part. Move it to a plate and break it into large chunks.",
    "Wipe the skillet clean and warm it over medium heat. Heat the tortillas one or two at a time for about 30 seconds per side, until soft and lightly toasted.",
    "Fill each tortilla with fish and top with slaw. Serve right away, 2 tacos per person."
